config BR2_PACKAGE_TAPO_C210_PTZ
	bool "tapo-c210-ptz"
	depends on BR2_arm
	select BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC_WEBUI_PTZ if BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC_WEBUI
	help
	  Board support for the TP-Link Tapo C210 v2 / C220 PTZ camera
	  (SigmaStar SSC333 + SmartSens SC3338 + 4-phase stepper motors).

	  Installs:
	  - /usr/sbin/ptz-controller: C motion engine implementing a quadratic
	    trapezoidal velocity profile (T_start=12ms, T_cruise=2.5ms, N_ramp=32),
	    soft-touch homing calibration, persistent coordinate & phase state
	    (/tmp/ptz_state & /etc/ptz_presets.json), and named/numbered presets.
	  - /usr/bin/gpio-motors: Symlink to /usr/sbin/ptz-controller providing
	    drop-in compatibility for legacy gpio-motors invocations.
	  - /usr/lib/majestic-af.so: Majestic PTZ plugin shim enabling Port-80
	    ONVIF PTZ and extending /onvif/ptz_service with GetPresets, GotoPreset,
	    SetPreset, RemovePreset, GotoHomePosition, RelativeMove, AbsoluteMove.
	  - /usr/sbin/onvif_simple_server: Standalone ONVIF Profile S/T PTZ SOAP
	    service configured via /etc/onvif_simple_server.conf and started by
	    /etc/init.d/S96onvif.
	  - /var/www/cgi-bin/j/ptz.cgi: Extended WebUI/REST PTZ CGI handler.
